e><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FUWA, KOH</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HORI, HIROAKI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KITABAYASHI, TETSUO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MAEHIRA, KEN</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NIHON SHINKU GIJUTSU KABUSHIKI KAISHA</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TATENO, NORIAKI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TOTO LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>UCHIMURA, TAKESHI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>FUWA KOH</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HORI HIROAKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KITABAYASHI TETSUO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MAEHIRA KEN</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TATENO NORIAKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>UCHIMURA TAKESHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FUWA, KOH</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HORI, HIROAKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KITABAYASHI, TETSUO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MAEHIRA, KEN</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TATENO, NORIAKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>UCHIMURA, TAKESHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>An electrostatic chuck for insulating substrate attraction, comprising a dielectric substrate (1a) acting on one surface thereof as an attraction surface of an insulating substrate and provided on the other surface with a plurality of electrodes (7) in order to electrostatic-attracting an insulating substrate such as a glass substrate, an insulating support base (1b) for fixing the dielectric substrate, a plurality of conducting terminals provided on the insulating support base, and a means for electrically connecting the electrodes with the conducting terminals, wherein a resistivity at room temperature of the dielectric substrate is up to 10&lt;13&gt;  OMEGA cm, a thickness of the dielectric substrate up to 2 mm, a width of an electrode up to 4 mm, and an interval between electrodes up to 2 mm. A heating/cooling plate (6), a gas supply piping for supplying gas to a gap between the insulating substrate and the attraction surface, and a temperature control system for controlling the temperature of the insulating substrate are added to the above electrostatic chuck for insulating substrate attraction to constitute an insulating substrate treating device.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Cette invention concerne un mandrin électrostatique assurant une isolation contre l'attraction du substrat, lequel comprend un substrat diélectrique (1a) dont une des surfaces sert de surface d'attraction d'un substrat isolant, et dont l'autre surface comprend plusieurs électrodes (7) afin d'attirer électrostatiquement un substrat isolant tel qu'un substrat en verre. Ce mandrin comprend également une base de support isolante (1b) servant à fixer le substrat diélectrique, plusieurs bornes conductrices formées sur la base de support isolante, ainsi qu'un système de connexion électrique des électrodes aux bornes conductrices. La résistivité du substrat diélectrique à température ambiante peut atteindre 10&lt;13&gt;  OMEGA cm, tandis que son épaisseur peut atteindre 2 mm, que la largeur d'une électrode peut atteindre 4 mm et que l'intervalle entre les électrodes peut atteindre 2 mm. Une plaque de chauffage/refroidissement (6), un tuyau d'alimentation en gaz vers le jour séparant le substrat isolant et la surface d'attraction, ainsi qu'un système de réglage de la température du substrat isolant sont en outre ajoutés au mandrin électrostatique qui assure une isolation contre l'attraction du substrat, ceci afin de former un dispositif de traitement à substrat isolant.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>